[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Good News]
[00:13.11]What was the good news?
[00:17.94]The secretary told me that
[00:57.15]Mr. Harmsworth would see me.
[00:24.42]I felt very nervous when I went into his office.
[00:29.06]He did not look up from his desk when I entered.
[00:33.31]After I had sat down,
[00:35.68]he said that business was very bad.
[00:40.60]He told me that the firm could not afford to pay such large salaries.
[00:48.79]Twenty people had already left.
[00:52.31]I knew that my turn had come.
[00:57.14]'Mr. Harmsworth,' I said in a weak voice.
[01:03.55]'Don't interrupt,' he said.
[01:07.62]Then he smiled and told me
[01:10.76]I would receive
[01:11.87]an extra thousand pounds a year!
